1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,697
Chapter 3. The fever and the burial.

2
00:00:03,997 --> 00:00:12,148
In 1977, Atari launched a cartridge console: one machine, all the games you could want.

3
00:00:12,328 --> 00:00:23,800
Arcades filled with lights and noise. By 1983, home video games were generating $3.2 billion in the United States.

4
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:27,217
And then, everything came crashing down.

5
00:00:27,397 --> 00:00:35,096
Too many consoles. Too many rushed games. People lost trust… and stopped buying.

6
00:00:35,276 --> 00:00:45,238
In September 1983, Atari trucks dumped unsold cartridges of E.T. and other games into a landfill in the New Mexico desert.

7
00:00:45,418 --> 00:00:51,531
By 1985, the market had plunged nearly 97%.

8
00:00:52,281 --> 00:00:56,507
Analysts said it was just a fad. And that it was over.
